I reach over and touch it , then it doesn 't seem so lonely anymore .

247
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:33,900
A crazy kid .

248
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:45,200
I do love you , Darlin ' .

249
00:26:58,400 --> 00:27:02,400
See you Thursday . - Goodbye , Honey .

250
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:08,200
You know I 'm not leaving here until you 're locked safely inside .

251
00:27:08,300 --> 00:27:12,300
All right , Darling .

252
00:27:21,700 --> 00:27:26,100
If you 're especially nice I may even lock the side door .

253
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:30,200
And be sure you keep the yard lights on .

254
00:27:51,100 --> 00:27:54,500
You 're mighty silent this trip , Jeff .

255
00:27:54,500 --> 00:27:56,400
You haven 't spoken ten words since takeoff .

256
00:27:56,500 --> 00:27:59,700
I guess I 'm preoccupied , Danny .

257
00:27:59,700 --> 00:28:02,700
We 've got thirty-three passengers back there that have time to be preoccupied .

258
00:28:02,800 --> 00:28:06,200
Flying this flybird doesn 't give you that opportunity .

259
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:09,400
I guess you 're right , Danny .

260
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:12,600
Paula ? - Yeah .

261
00:28:12,600 --> 00:28:15,700
There 's nothing wrong between you two ? - Oh no , nothing like that .

262
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:17,535
Just that I 'm worried , she being there alone and

263
00:28:17,635 --> 00:28:19,300
those strange things flying over the house and

264
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:24,100
those incidents in the graveyard the past few days . It 's just got me worried .

265
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:26,757
Well , I haven 't figured out those crazy skybirds

266
00:28:26,857 --> 00:28:28,800
yet but I give you fifty to one odds

267
00:28:28,900 --> 00:28:31,200
the police have figured out that cemetery thing by now .

268
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:32,300
I hope so .

269
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:35,500
If you 're really that worried Jeff why don 't you radio in and find out ?

270
00:28:35,600 --> 00:28:37,719
Mac should be on duty at the field by now .

271
00:28:37,819 --> 00:28:40,300
He could call Paula and relay the message to you .

272
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:41,400
Hi Edith .

273
00:28:41,500 --> 00:28:44,900
Hi Silents . I haven 't heard a word from this end of the plane since we left the field .

274
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:47,900
Jeff 's been giving me and himself a study in silence .

275
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:51,100
You boys are feudin ' ? - Oh no Edie , nothing like that .

276
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:53,800
Hey Edie , how about you and me balling [ bawling ? ] it up in Albuquerque ?

277
00:28:53,900 --> 00:28:56,300
Albuquerque ? Have you read that flight schedule Boy ?

278
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:57,400
What about it ?

279
00:28:57,500 --> 00:29:01,600
We land in Albuquerque at 4 am . That 's strictly a nine o 'clock town .

280
00:29:01,700 --> 00:29:03,900
Well I know a friend that 'll help us - - ...

281
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:07,300
Let 's have a problem first , huh Danny . - Ah he 's worried about Paula .

282
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:10,194
I read about that cemetery business .

283
00:29:10,294 --> 00:29:15,300
I tried to get you kids to not buy too near one of those things .

284
00:29:15,400 --> 00:29:17,000
He thought it 'd be quiet and peaceful there .

285
00:29:17,100 --> 00:29:21,520
No doubt about that . It 's quiet alright , like a tomb .

286
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:23,900
I 'm sorry Jeff , that was a bad joke .

287
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:26,092
Say . , I almost forgot what I came in here for .

288
00:29:26,192 --> 00:29:27,400
How 's the coffee situation ?

289
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:30,500
Mmmm that 's for me . - That sure wouldn 't hurt anything , Edie .

290
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:35,000
Okay , I 'll be right back . And say Jeff , make that call to your wife .

291
00:29:35,100 --> 00:29:38,100
Huh , not only will she throw water on my Albuquerque plan but now she 's

292
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:39,200
repeating herself .

293
00:29:39,300 --> 00:29:45,250
How ' bout that Albuquerque ball ? - I can 't resist your charm , Danny Boy .

294
00:29:49,500 --> 00:29:54,500
Residents near the cemetery paid little attention to the blast of thunder

295
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:57,300
and the flash of lightning .

296
00:29:57,300 --> 00:30:02,740
But from the blast , arose the moving figure of the dead old man .

297
00:30:30,500 --> 00:30:34,500
Hello ? Who ?

298
00:30:34,600 --> 00:30:38,600
Mac ? Well , hi Mac .

299
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Sure I 'm all right .

300
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:43,000
I just fell asleep .

301
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:48,600
Tell Jeff I 'm all right .

302
00:30:48,600 --> 00:30:52,600
Okay Mac . Thanks for calling . Goodnight .

303
00:34:16,200 --> 00:34:20,200
Mrs. Trent . Mrs. Trent . What 's wrong ?

304
00:36:34,300 --> 00:36:37,655
They 'll be at the hatch in a moment . You can open it now , Tanna .

305
00:36:59,400 --> 00:37:02,180
Turn off the electrodes quickly . They can 't tell us from anyone else .

306
00:37:28,500 --> 00:37:31,000
It 's tough to find something when you don 't know what you 're looking for .

307
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:32,968
I don 't think the Lieutenant does either .

308
00:37:33,068 --> 00:37:35,500
Then what 're doing out here ? I was off duty an hour ago .

309
00:37:35,500 --> 00:37:39,315
Ah don 't ask me any questions . I 'm just a hardhand [ hat ? head ? ] just like you .

310
00:37:47,900 --> 00:37:49,500
What do you suppose that noise was ?

311
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:51,533
Whatever it was it 's no more strange than the

312
00:37:51,633 --> 00:37:53,400
other things happening around this cemetery .

313
00:37:53,500 --> 00:37:56,800
Spirits like Old Farmer Caulder talked about .

314
00:37:56,900 --> 00:37:57,900
Heh . Maybe .

315
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:01,000
The only spirits he saw tonight were those I smelled on his breath .

316
00:38:01,100 --> 00:38:03,262
Well don 't forget Mrs. Trent claims to have seen them too .

317
00:38:03,362 --> 00:38:04,800
She didn 't have anything on her breath .

318
00:38:04,900 --> 00:38:05,980
She was hysterical .

319
00:38:06,080 --> 00:38:09,300
Well true , she was frightened , and in a state of shock .

320
00:38:09,400 --> 00:38:14,400
But , don 't forget that torn nightgown and the scratched feet .

321
00:38:14,500 --> 00:38:16,820
Yeah I hadn 't thought of that .

322
00:38:16,920 --> 00:38:20,900
I guess that 's why you 're a detective lieutenant

323
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:23,500
and I 'm still a uniformed cop .

324
00:38:23,600 --> 00:38:25,900
Sometimes it 's only the breaks , Larry . In the meantime let 's get - ...

325
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:28,800
Lieutenant , Lieutenant . Did you hear that ? - How could we help it ?

326
00:38:28,900 --> 00:38:30,700
It sure was strange . - Know what it was ?

327
00:38:30,800 --> 00:38:31,800
No more than you do .

328
00:38:31,900 --> 00:38:34,100
If it weren 't for orders I 'd get out of here right now .

329
00:38:34,200 --> 00:38:34,796
It was a saucer .

330
00:38:34,896 --> 00:38:36,500
A flying saucer ? What makes you say that ?

331
00:38:36,600 --> 00:38:39,100
You remember the noise we heard the other night ?

332
00:38:39,200 --> 00:38:41,600
We were knocked to the ground , how could I forget ?

333
00:38:41,700 --> 00:38:45,400
Exactly , but you 're not remembering that sound .

334
00:38:45,500 --> 00:38:47,166
There you 're wrong , Lieutenant .

335
00:38:47,266 --> 00:38:51,200
I 'm with a fact the sound is similar , but what about the blinding light ?

336
00:38:51,300 --> 00:38:55,100
Well haven 't you heard ? Many times a saucer hasn 't had a glow ,

337
00:38:55,200 --> 00:39:00,300
or a light of any kind for that matter . - That proves it . What next Lietenant ?

338
00:39:00,400 --> 00:39:02,170
Maybe this doesn 't mean much ,

339
00:39:02,270 --> 00:39:06,800
but uh Jamie and me found a grave that looks like it 's been busting into .

340
00:39:06,900 --> 00:39:07,900
What ? Where ? - Why uh why ...

341
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:11,400
Come on man out with it , we haven 't got all day to waste .

342
00:39:11,500 --> 00:39:17,025
Uh , just over there beyond the crypt . - All right , show us the way .

343
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:21,400
Look , here it is Lieutenant .

344
00:39:24,200 --> 00:39:26,500
Ah it 's been broken into all right .

345
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:31,900
Strange . If someone had broken in , the dirt should be piled up here somewhere .

346
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:34,439
It looks like it 's fallen in into the grave .

347
00:39:34,539 --> 00:39:37,600
Larry you 'll be out of that uniform before you know it .

348
00:39:37,700 --> 00:39:40,491
Do we have the right to look down there Lieutenant ?

349
00:39:40,591 --> 00:39:41,600
Ah , technically no .

350
00:39:41,700 --> 00:39:43,771
Well , this spot looks familiar , though .

351
00:39:43,871 --> 00:39:47,900
We shouldn 't investigate any further without the permission of next of kin .

352
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:49,200
Let 's go get it .

353
00:39:49,300 --> 00:39:50,300
How ?

354
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:53,500
I see what you mean , the gravestone 's down there .

355
00:39:53,600 --> 00:39:56,000
Well , let 's go down and find out who 's grave it is .

356
00:39:56,100 --> 00:39:59,900
How ? - By going down and finding out .

357
00:39:59,900 --> 00:40:03,900
Are you sure you mean that Lieutenant ? - If I didn 't mean it I wouldn 't have said it .

358
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:05,000
Scared ?

359
00:40:05,100 --> 00:40:08,400
Well , why do I always get hooked up with these spook details ?

360
00:40:08,500 --> 00:40:12,000
Monsters , graves , bodies ,

361
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:14,000
oooh all right .

362
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:25,700
Casket 's here , but nobody 's in it .

363
00:40:25,700 --> 00:40:29,500
Can you read the name on the casket ?

364
00:40:29,500 --> 00:40:32,800
It 's too dark . Give me a flashlight .

365
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:37,730
How ' bout a match ? - We sure could try it . Let me have them .

366
00:40:46,900 --> 00:40:50,900
It 's Inspector Clay 's grave . But he ain 't in it .

367
00:40:56,800 --> 00:41:01,135
But meanwhile , in the Pentagon , in Washington DC ...

368
00:41:06,700 --> 00:41:10,400
Try G2 ...

369
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:17,000
Yes of course , I 'll keep in touch .

370
00:41:18,700 --> 00:41:24,400
Come in , Colonel Edwards . Close the door . At ease , Colonel .

371
00:41:24,400 --> 00:41:28,100
Thank you , Sir . - Sit down .

372
00:41:31,100 --> 00:41:36,500
I understand , Colonel , you 've been on tap for many of our saucer attacks .

373
00:41:36,600 --> 00:41:40,200
I 'm in charge of field operations , Sir .

374
00:41:40,200 --> 00:41:44,400
You believe there are such things as flying saucers , Colonel ?

375
00:41:44,500 --> 00:41:46,700
Yessir . - You 've seen them ?

376
00:41:46,700 --> 00:41:48,400
Yessir .

377
00:41:48,500 --> 00:41:51,105
You realize there 's a government directive

378
00:41:51,205 --> 00:41:54,400
stating that there is no such thing as a flying saucer ?

379
00:41:54,500 --> 00:41:56,000
Yessir .

380
00:41:56,100 --> 00:41:59,300
Do you stand by your statement that you 've seen flying saucers ?

381
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:02,800
Well , uh

382
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:05,600
yessir .

383
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:10,600
This could mean a court marshall . Admitting this against direct orders .

384
00:42:10,700 --> 00:42:14,100
General Roberts , may I speak freely ?

385
00:42:14,100 --> 00:42:15,100
You may .

386
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:17,000
How could I hope to hold down my command

387
00:42:17,100 --> 00:42:21,265
if I didn 't believe in what I saw and shot at ?

388
00:42:23,100 --> 00:42:27,100
I , uh , like you Colonel . - Thank you , Sir .

389
00:42:27,900 --> 00:42:31,900
There are flying saucers .

390
00:42:33,200 --> 00:42:38,200
There 's no doubt they are in our skies . They 've been there for some time .

391
00:42:38,300 --> 00:42:39,800
What 're we going to do about them ?

392
00:42:39,900 --> 00:42:43,600
Who knows ? - Then , uh , they really are there ?

393
00:42:43,600 --> 00:42:47,600
I thought you were convinced of that . - I am .

394
00:42:47,800 --> 00:42:49,900
We 've had contact with them .

395
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:52,900
Contact ? How ? - Radio .

396
00:42:52,900 --> 00:42:55,900
They speak our language ? - Well not quite .

397
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:58,779
We received messages from their space ships .

398
00:42:58,879 --> 00:43:02,300
For a while it came in as just a lot of jumbled noise .

399
00:43:02,400 --> 00:43:04,100
And now , Sir ?

400
00:43:04,200 --> 00:43:07,680
Well since they first uh tried contact with us by radio ,

401
00:43:07,780 --> 00:43:10,000
we 've developed a language computer .

402
00:43:10,100 --> 00:43:13,900
A machine that breaks down any language to our own .

403
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:18,000
General , uh , what 's this all got to do with me ?

404
00:43:18,500 --> 00:43:22,400
Well you 've been in charge of saucer field activity for a long while .

405
00:43:22,500 --> 00:43:26,300
I think it 's about time you heard these recordings . Do you mind ?

406
00:43:26,400 --> 00:43:30,400
Mind ? Huh , I 'm anxious .

407
00:43:36,600 --> 00:43:41,615
This is Eros , a space soldier from a planet of your galaxy .

408
00:43:41,700 --> 00:43:46,900
I fully realize our language differences , however I also know you finally have

409
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:51,139
perfected the dictorobitary , or as you on Earth put it ,

410
00:43:51,239 --> 00:43:56,100
the language computer . So you can now understand that which I speak .

411
00:43:56,200 --> 00:44:00,300
Since the beginning of your time , we have been far beyond your planet .

412
00:44:00,400 --> 00:44:07,370
It has taken you centuries to even grasp what we developed eons of your years ago .

413
00:44:07,600 --> 00:44:10,168
Do you still believe it impossible we exist ?

414
00:44:10,268 --> 00:44:14,800
You didn 't actually think you were the only inhabited planet in the universe ?

415
00:44:14,900 --> 00:44:17,600
How can any race be so stupid ?

416
00:44:17,600 --> 00:44:20,245
Permit me to set your mind at ease .

417
00:44:20,345 --> 00:44:24,300
We do not want to conquer your planet . Only save it .

418
00:44:24,400 --> 00:44:29,400
We could have destroyed it long ago , if that had been our aim .

419
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:31,383
Our principal purpose is friendly .

420
00:44:31,483 --> 00:44:34,900
I admit , we have had to take certain means which you might

421
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:37,200
refer to as criminal ,

422
00:44:37,200 --> 00:44:39,233
but that is because of your big guns

423
00:44:39,333 --> 00:44:41,900
which have destroyed some of our representatives .

424
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:45,418
If you persist in denying us our landings ,

425
00:44:45,518 --> 00:44:51,000
then we must only accept that you do not want us on friendly terms .

426
00:44:51,100 --> 00:44:56,800
We then have no alternative but to destroy you before you destroy us .

427
00:44:56,900 --> 00:45:00,935
With your ancient , juvenile minds , you have developed explosives

428
00:45:01,035 --> 00:45:04,400
too fast for your minds to conceive what you were doing .

429
00:45:04,500 --> 00:45:08,600
You are on the verge of destroying the entire universe .

430
00:45:08,700 --> 00:45:10,700
We are part of that universe .

431
00:45:10,800 --> 00:45:12,800
This is our last -

432
00:45:17,300 --> 00:45:18,777
That 's the end of that one .

433
00:45:18,877 --> 00:45:22,900
Atmospheric conditions in outer space often interfere with transmitting .

434
00:45:23,000 --> 00:45:25,400
How many of these recordings do you have General ?

435
00:45:25,500 --> 00:45:27,949
An even dozen up to now . This was the last one .

436
00:45:28,049 --> 00:45:29,700
We received it over a month ago .

437
00:45:29,800 --> 00:45:35,665
Do you think they mean business ? - We can 't afford to take any chances .

438
00:45:37,800 --> 00:45:39,600
Come over here . You ever been to Hollywood ?

439
00:45:39,700 --> 00:45:43,500
Oh a couple of times . A few years ago . - You 're going to be there in the morning .

440
00:45:43,600 --> 00:45:46,467
Just a few minutes from Hollywood , in the

441
00:45:46,567 --> 00:45:49,500
town of San Fernando , reports have come in

442
00:45:49,600 --> 00:45:54,300
of saucers flying so low the exhaust knocked people to the ground .

443
00:45:54,400 --> 00:45:58,800
There have even been stated claims of saucer landings .

444
00:45:58,900 --> 00:46:02,500
Major Carlson will replace you while you 're out there .

445
00:46:02,600 --> 00:46:05,800
You 're the best man for the job of attempting to contact them .

446
00:46:05,900 --> 00:46:09,600
Find them , Colonel . See what in hell it is they want .

447
00:46:09,700 --> 00:46:11,700
All right , Sir .

448
00:46:16,600 --> 00:46:20,100
These are confidential reports , Colonel . Read them over carefully on the plane ,

449
00:46:20,200 --> 00:46:23,415
turn them over to intelligence when you get to Los Angeles .

450
00:46:23,515 --> 00:46:25,900
They 'll have further orders for disposition .

451
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:28,000
Yessir .

452
00:46:29,500 --> 00:46:32,200
Colonel Edwards ? - Yessir ?

453
00:46:32,200 --> 00:46:34,410
Good luck . - Thank you , Sir .

454
00:47:03,300 --> 00:47:05,100
We are ready to report , Excellency .

455
00:47:05,200 --> 00:47:09,200
You are many days late . - It was unavoidable .

456
00:47:09,200 --> 00:47:11,965
We tried to transmit via televisor , but atmospheric

457
00:47:12,065 --> 00:47:14,100
conditions made transmission impossible .

458
00:47:14,200 --> 00:47:17,150
You should have transmitted as soon as conditions permitted .

459
00:47:17,250 --> 00:47:18,900
I thought time was of the essence .

460
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:21,033
Suspicion has fallen upon our movements .

461
00:47:21,133 --> 00:47:24,000
Our ships have been viewed near the point of operations .

462
00:47:24,100 --> 00:47:27,100
And what has this extra time gained , Eros ?

463
00:47:27,200 --> 00:47:31,100
We have successfully risen three of the dead ones .

464
00:47:31,200 --> 00:47:34,200
Permit me to see one . - Bring in the big one .

465
00:47:34,300 --> 00:47:38,300
Use your small electrode gun .

466
00:47:41,200 --> 00:47:43,400
I have taken two ships from your command .

467
00:47:43,500 --> 00:47:47,000
But ... that will leave only my ship .

468
00:47:47,000 --> 00:47:50,900
It is necessary that you continue your mission alone .

469
00:47:51,000 --> 00:47:54,900
I have need of your other ships elsewhere .

470
00:47:54,900 --> 00:47:58,660
Even though you have risen three of the Earth dead ,

471
00:47:58,760 --> 00:48:01,100
the plan is far from successful ,

472
00:48:01,200 --> 00:48:04,100
and you Eros , must prove it an operational success before

473
00:48:04,200 --> 00:48:05,200
more time ,

474
00:48:05,300 --> 00:48:10,200
energy , and ships , may be spent on it .

475
00:48:11,700 --> 00:48:14,400
We will not fail . Everything is on our side .

476
00:48:14,500 --> 00:48:19,005
Not everything . You do not have the live Earth people .

477
00:48:23,900 --> 00:48:28,200
You report that your ship was viewed at scene of your present operations ?

478
00:48:28,300 --> 00:48:30,300
That is correct .

479
00:48:30,600 --> 00:48:34,800
They have been viewed many times , but not at the scene of operations .

480
00:48:34,900 --> 00:48:37,790
Something must be done about that .

481
00:48:44,100 --> 00:48:48,200
Stop him Tanna . He 's close enough . Turn off your electrode gun .

482
00:48:48,300 --> 00:48:52,300
No . No . Stop him Tanna .

483
00:48:53,200 --> 00:48:55,700
I can 't get it , it 's jammed . - Stop him you fool .

484
00:48:55,800 --> 00:49:01,070
Drop the gun to the floor , Tanna . The metal will break contact .

485
00:49:06,300 --> 00:49:08,800
[ Gasping ] That was too close .

486
00:49:08,800 --> 00:49:10,800
Yes .

487
00:49:14,500 --> 00:49:19,345
Bring the giant here that I may get a better look at him .

488
00:49:30,800 --> 00:49:35,600
Yes , he 's a fine specimen . Are they all this powerful on planet Earth ?

489
00:49:35,700 --> 00:49:38,400
This one is an exception , Excellency .

490
00:49:38,500 --> 00:49:43,200
What are the other two like ? - One is a woman , the other an old man .

491
00:49:43,300 --> 00:49:46,500
An old man , you say ? - Yes , Excellency .

492
00:49:50,300 --> 00:49:54,200
This gives me a plan . Put the big one away .

493
00:49:54,200 --> 00:49:55,675
Pick up your electrode gun .

494
00:49:55,775 --> 00:49:59,000
Make sure it 's in working order before pointing it at him .

495
00:49:59,100 --> 00:50:01,300
Whatever made it jam must have been cleared by the fall .

496
00:50:01,400 --> 00:50:03,610
Take him back to the ship .

497
00:50:14,600 --> 00:50:19,279
The old one must be sacrificed . Re-land on Earth .

498
00:50:19,379 --> 00:50:22,900
Send the old one to enter a dwelling .

499
00:50:24,100 --> 00:50:29,100
Then cut off the electrokinetic and turn on your ship 's decomposure ray .

500
00:50:29,200 --> 00:50:34,388
The result will astound those watching . Astound them enough to delay their

501
00:50:34,488 --> 00:50:39,200
attention until you have gained your other recruits from the cemetery .

502
00:50:39,300 --> 00:50:42,600
Yes , Excellency . It 'll be done .

503
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:46,425
Report to me when this has been accomplished .

504
00:50:52,900 --> 00:50:57,000
Eros , the Earth people are getting to that which we fear .

505
00:50:57,100 --> 00:51:00,700
Since they will not listen or respect our existence ,

506
00:51:00,800 --> 00:51:02,896
they cannot help but believe our powers when

507
00:51:02,996 --> 00:51:05,000
they see their own dead walking ' round again ,

508
00:51:05,100 --> 00:51:07,750
brought about by our advancement in such things .

509
00:51:07,850 --> 00:51:10,500
As soon as you have enough of the dead recruits ,

510
00:51:10,600 --> 00:51:17,602
march them on the capitals of the Earth , let nothing stand in your way . Their own

511
00:51:17,702 --> 00:51:24,587
dead will be used to make them accept our existence , and believe in that fact .

512
00:52:02,700 --> 00:52:06,600
Mr. and Mrs. Trent ... this is Colonel Edwards from Washington DC .

513
00:52:06,700 --> 00:52:09,000
Good evening , Colonel . - Hello Colonel .

514
00:52:09,100 --> 00:52:11,200
Colonel would like to ask you a few questions .

515
00:52:11,300 --> 00:52:15,720
Questions ? What about , Colonel ? - May I , uh , sit down ?

516
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:18,200
Oh , I 'm sorry , please do .

517
00:52:18,200 --> 00:52:22,313
I want to ask you about your strange experience

518
00:52:22,413 --> 00:52:26,300
the other night , when you saw the flying saucer .

519
00:52:26,400 --> 00:52:29,300
After that the police brought me home .

520
00:52:29,400 --> 00:52:32,800
I hope I never see such a sight again .

521
00:52:32,800 --> 00:52:36,100
Well after your description I don 't think I 'd want to see it either .

522
00:52:36,200 --> 00:52:37,200
One thing

523
00:52:37,300 --> 00:52:40,300
more ... after you were forced to the ground by that blast of wind ,

524
00:52:40,400 --> 00:52:46,000
was it a hot or cold blast ? - It 's kind of hard to explain .

525
00:52:46,000 --> 00:52:49,502
It wasn 't hot , wasn 't cold , it was just a terrific

526
00:52:49,602 --> 00:52:52,300
force . We-we couldn 't get off the ground .

527
00:52:52,400 --> 00:52:56,300
The light blinded me so badly I couldn 't see a thing .

528
00:52:56,400 --> 00:53:00,599
We could only feel the pressure of the wind , until it was gone .

529
00:53:00,699 --> 00:53:02,200
When the glare left us ,

530
00:53:02,300 --> 00:53:05,200
we could see a glowing ball disappearing off in the distance .

531
00:53:05,300 --> 00:53:07,935
Which way ? - Toward the cemetery .

532
00:53:23,700 --> 00:53:27,200
This is the most fantastic story I 've ever heard .

533
00:53:27,300 --> 00:53:29,100
And every word of it 's true , too .

534
00:53:29,200 --> 00:53:31,500
That 's the fantastic part of it .

535
00:53:31,600 --> 00:53:35,800
We found a lot of suspicious things out in that cemetery .

536
00:53:35,900 --> 00:53:41,340
Then again , didn 't find anything to base a fact or suspicion on .

537
00:53:41,400 --> 00:53:45,400
Hey , do you hear anything .

538
00:53:51,300 --> 00:53:53,700
You see anything out there Kelton ?

539
00:53:53,800 --> 00:53:57,600
Too dark , Lieutenant .

540
00:53:57,600 --> 00:54:01,600
But something 's started stinking awful bad .

541
00:54:08,100 --> 00:54:12,100
There 's something out there .

542
00:55:39,300 --> 00:55:41,142
What do you make of that ?

543
00:55:41,242 --> 00:55:44,900
You got me . It didn 't look that way a minute ago .

544
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:46,675
What about your man ?

545
00:55:46,775 --> 00:55:50,865
Oh , in the excitement I forgot all about Kelton .

546
00:55:56,100 --> 00:55:59,500
Oh , he 'll be all right in a few minutes .

547
00:56:00,300 --> 00:56:03,300
Did you see that thing ? Did you get it ? - We got it .

548
00:56:03,400 --> 00:56:07,200
What was it ? It didn 't fall ... I fired every bullet I had .

549
00:56:07,300 --> 00:56:12,800
So did I. I don 't know what it was or what happened , but unless that bag of bones

550
00:56:12,900 --> 00:56:17,490
can reassemble itself , it 's out of the running now .

551
00:56:27,600 --> 00:56:31,100
Colonel I 've been out here so often you 'd think I 'd taken a lease on this place .

552
00:56:31,200 --> 00:56:33,100
Not a long lease , I hope .

553
00:56:33,200 --> 00:56:37,100
I see what you mean . But you know , I can 't help but feel the answer 's out here

554
00:56:37,200 --> 00:56:38,200
somewhere .

555
00:56:38,300 --> 00:56:40,300
Is the uh girl safe ?

556
00:56:41,200 --> 00:56:47,000
Mrs. Trent you 'd better stay with the car . - Stay here alone ? Not on your life .

557
00:56:47,100 --> 00:56:48,100
Modern women ...

558
00:56:48,200 --> 00:56:50,100
Yeah , they been that way all down through the ages .

559
00:56:50,200 --> 00:56:52,900
Especially in a spot like this .

560
00:56:52,900 --> 00:56:54,900
Kelton . - Yessir ? - Stay with Mrs. Trent .

561
00:56:55,000 --> 00:56:56,600
All right , Lieutenant .

562
00:56:56,700 --> 00:57:02,310
Now you stay close to the officer , Honey . - I 'd feel safer with you .

563
00:57:04,700 --> 00:57:07,226
Now the Lieutenant knows best .

564
00:57:07,326 --> 00:57:13,030
Oh I don 't like it , but I guess there isn 't much I can do about it .

565
00:57:17,000 --> 00:57:19,500
You have a gun ? - No .

566
00:57:19,500 --> 00:57:21,500
Know how to use one ?

567
00:57:21,900 --> 00:57:25,045
After four years in the Marine Corps ?

568
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:28,200
Here . - You think we 'll need these ?

569
00:57:28,300 --> 00:57:31,360
You can never tell . Let 's get going .

570
00:57:51,600 --> 00:57:52,938
What do you expect to find out here ?

571
00:57:53,038 --> 00:57:54,800
Well there 's only one answer to that Mr. Trent ,

572
00:57:54,900 --> 00:57:59,800
we 'll know when we find it . Inspector Clay 's grave is right over here .

573
00:57:59,900 --> 00:58:02,965
Is that the one you told me was broken into ?

574
00:58:03,065 --> 00:58:05,065
Yes .

575
00:58:20,900 --> 00:58:22,500
This it ? - Yeah .

576
00:58:22,600 --> 00:58:25,200
Looks to me like someone had broken out instead of in .

577
00:58:25,300 --> 00:58:28,847
I figured that , but that 's impossible . - I wonder .

578
00:58:28,947 --> 00:58:32,200
Look , Colonel , some things just can 't happen .

579
00:58:32,300 --> 00:58:35,753
Yeah well after that apparition that was draped across Mr. Trent 's

580
00:58:35,853 --> 00:58:38,900
patio , I would say we should keep our minds open to anything .

581
00:58:39,000 --> 00:58:42,900
Look , Colonel , I 'm a policeman . I 've got to deal in facts .

582
00:58:43,000 --> 00:58:48,386
But , I guess I 'll have to go along with you . You know I bet my

583
00:58:48,486 --> 00:58:53,756
badge right now we haven 't seen the last of those weirdies .

584
00:58:56,000 --> 00:58:59,400
They 'll discover our ship soon . - You going to let them find us ?

585
00:58:59,500 --> 00:59:03,800
It 's the only way . These are the same men who have been so close so often .

586
00:59:03,900 --> 00:59:06,700
They must be halted before they can inform others about us .

587
00:59:06,800 --> 00:59:11,475
But there were others in the car . - They 'll be taken too .

588
00:59:13,100 --> 00:59:17,977
Send the big one to get the girl and the policeman . I 'll

589
00:59:18,077 --> 00:59:23,007
turn on the dictorobitary so we may converse with them .

590
00:59:49,400 --> 00:59:52,100
You know , maybe we 're barking up the wrong tree .

591
00:59:52,200 --> 00:59:55,100
One thing a policeman learns , Mr. Trent , is patience .

592
00:59:55,200 --> 01:00:00,045
Where the burn spot you mentioned . - Right over the - look .

593
01:00:09,900 --> 01:00:13,130
We 'll investigate , but move carefully .

594
01:00:56,300 --> 01:01:01,200
A moment or two more , and you will be the first live Earth people

595
01:01:01,300 --> 01:01:04,190
ever to enter a celestial ship .

596
01:01:04,700 --> 01:01:10,055
Wow ... boy , how could anything that big hide for so long a time ?

597
01:01:11,200 --> 01:01:13,900
Never heard metal sound like that before .

598
01:01:14,000 --> 01:01:15,000
What do you see ?

599
01:01:15,100 --> 01:01:18,600
Only my reflection . Must be some kind of one-way glass .

600
01:01:18,700 --> 01:01:24,140
How do you get into this thing ? - I 'm not sure I want to find out .

601
01:01:35,300 --> 01:01:37,300
They 're just outside .

602
01:01:42,500 --> 01:01:45,305
You can open the outer hatch now .

603
01:02:00,600 --> 01:02:03,600
You goin ' in that thing ? - That 's what we 're here for .

604
01:02:03,700 --> 01:02:06,278
I don 't know , the way these things speed around

605
01:02:06,378 --> 01:02:08,850
we might just get in there and pft . Off it goes .

606
01:02:08,950 --> 01:02:10,200
That 's a chance we take .

607
01:02:10,300 --> 01:02:13,059
Well , I took a chance on those earlier airplanes . Might just as well

608
01:02:13,159 --> 01:02:15,800
see what the inside of one of these looks like . Got your guns ready ?

609
01:02:15,900 --> 01:02:20,522
I tell you one thing , if a little green man jumps out

610
01:02:20,622 --> 01:02:25,297
at me I 'm shooting first and asking questions later .

611
01:02:30,900 --> 01:02:33,705
They 're in the outer chamber now .

612
01:02:34,400 --> 01:02:38,400
Eros , do we have to kill them ?

613
01:02:39,800 --> 01:02:43,800
Yes . - It seems such a waste .

614
01:02:44,400 --> 01:02:49,542
Well wouldn 't it be better to kill a few now than , with their meddling , permit

615
01:02:49,642 --> 01:02:51,900
them to destroy the entire universe ?

616
01:02:52,000 --> 01:02:54,600
You 're always right , Eros . - Of course .

617
01:02:54,700 --> 01:02:59,885
But those are not my words , those are the words of the Ruler .

618
01:03:05,500 --> 01:03:08,815
Now you two stay right where you 're at .

619
01:03:12,500 --> 01:03:16,057
We will do as you command . For the moment .

620
01:03:16,157 --> 01:03:20,747
No for the moment about it . You just do as I tell you .

621
01:03:27,300 --> 01:03:31,200
You do not need guns . - Maybe we think we do .

622
01:03:31,200 --> 01:03:33,139
They would be of no use to you now .

623
01:03:33,239 --> 01:03:36,200
They 've been mighty useful before on flesh and blood ,

624
01:03:36,300 --> 01:03:40,295
and you two look like you 've got a lot of both .

625
01:03:41,800 --> 01:03:44,598
True , they would be effective upon us . If you

626
01:03:44,698 --> 01:03:47,200
were to have the opportunity to use them ...

627
01:03:47,300 --> 01:03:53,766
Mister , if you don 't get away from that control board I 'll show you just how

628
01:03:53,866 --> 01:03:55,991
effective they can be .

629
01:03:56,100 --> 01:04:00,200
Shall we talk now , or wait ? Your friends will be here shortly .

630
01:04:00,300 --> 01:04:04,040
What friends ? - Those you left at the vehicle .

631
01:04:04,800 --> 01:04:07,600
If you 've done anything to Paula ... - Take it easy Mr. Trent .

632
01:04:07,700 --> 01:04:13,140
Oh I assure you , no harm has come to her . Would you like to see ?

633
01:04:14,200 --> 01:04:16,735
Next time you try that I won 't aim at the board .

634
01:04:16,835 --> 01:04:18,400
You 're a headstrong young man .

635
01:04:18,500 --> 01:04:24,705
I was only going to turn on the televisor so you could see her movements .

636
01:04:25,500 --> 01:04:29,500
Go ahead , my friend , but move very carefully .

637
01:04:44,000 --> 01:04:46,000
She 's only fainted .

638
01:04:46,700 --> 01:04:50,500
You fiend . - I ? A fiend ? ...

639
01:04:50,500 --> 01:04:54,200
I am a soldier of our planet .

640
01:04:55,900 --> 01:05:01,700
I ? A fiend ? We did not come here as enemies .

641
01:05:02,600 --> 01:05:06,400
We came only with friendly intentions . To talk .

642
01:05:06,500 --> 01:05:08,000
To ask your aid .

643
01:05:08,100 --> 01:05:10,700
Our aid ? - Yes .

644
01:05:10,700 --> 01:05:14,328
Your aid for the whole universe . But your governments

645
01:05:14,428 --> 01:05:17,400
of Earth refused even to accept our existence .

646
01:05:17,500 --> 01:05:24,100
Even though you 've seen us , heard our messages , you still refused to accept us .

647
01:05:24,200 --> 01:05:28,000
Why is it so important that you want to contact the governments of our Earth ?

648
01:05:28,100 --> 01:05:32,690
Because of death . Because all you of Earth are idiots .

649
01:05:33,800 --> 01:05:37,300
Now you just hold on , Buster . - No you hold on .

650
01:05:37,400 --> 01:05:42,700
First was your firecracker , a harmless explosive . Then your handgrenade .

651
01:05:42,800 --> 01:05:49,800
They began to kill your own people a few at a time . Then the bomb , then a larger bomb .

652
01:05:49,900 --> 01:05:54,700
Many people are killed at one time . Then your scientists

653
01:05:54,800 --> 01:05:58,800
stumbled upon the atom bomb . Split the atom .

654
01:05:59,200 --> 01:06:04,810
Then the hydrogen bomb , where you actually explode the air itself .

655
01:06:04,900 --> 01:06:08,405
Now you [ audio jump ] brings the destruction

656
01:06:08,505 --> 01:06:11,700
of the entire universe , served by our sun .

657
01:06:11,800 --> 01:06:15,800
The only explosion left is the solaronite .

658
01:06:16,500 --> 01:06:19,700
Why there 's no such thing . - Perhaps to you .

659
01:06:19,800 --> 01:06:22,994
But we 've known it for centuries . Your scientists

660
01:06:23,094 --> 01:06:26,100
will stumble upon it as they have all the others .

661
01:06:26,200 --> 01:06:32,900
But the juvenile minds you possess will not comprehend its strength , until it 's too late .

662
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:36,000
You 're way above our heads .

663
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:40,500
The solaronite is a way to explode the actual particles of sunlight .

664
01:06:40,600 --> 01:06:42,900
Why that 's impossible .

665
01:06:42,900 --> 01:06:47,200
Even now , your scientists are working on a way to harness the sun 's rays .

666
01:06:47,300 --> 01:06:50,100
The rays of sunlight are minute particles .

667
01:06:50,200 --> 01:06:54,100
Is it so far from your imagination they cannot do as I have suggested ?

668
01:06:54,200 --> 01:06:57,400
Why a particle of sunlight can 't even be seen or measured .

669
01:06:57,500 --> 01:07:02,260
Can you see or measure an atom ? Yet you can explode one .

670
01:07:02,500 --> 01:07:05,300
A ray of sunlight is made up many atoms .

671
01:07:05,400 --> 01:07:07,526
So what if we do developed this solaronite

672
01:07:07,626 --> 01:07:09,800
bomb ? We 'd be even a stronger nation than now .

673
01:07:09,900 --> 01:07:15,900
Stronger . You see ? You see ? Your stupid minds ... stupid . Stupid .

674
01:07:16,100 --> 01:07:19,800
That 's all I 'm taking from you . - Get back here you jerk .

675
01:07:19,900 --> 01:07:21,900
Let him finish .

676
01:07:28,900 --> 01:07:32,100
It 's because of men like you that all must be destroyed .

677
01:07:32,200 --> 01:07:37,200
Headstrong , violent . No use of the mind God gave you .

678
01:07:38,000 --> 01:07:40,700
You talk of God ?

679
01:07:40,700 --> 01:07:45,970
You also think it impossible that we , too , might think of God ?

680
01:07:47,700 --> 01:07:54,925
You , who wear the uniform of your country . You see , I wear the uniform of my country .

681
01:07:55,800 --> 01:08:02,300
Yes , we 've had to use drastic means to get to you , but you left us no alternative .

682
01:08:02,400 --> 01:08:09,400
When you have the solaronite , you have nothing . Nor , does the universe .

683
01:08:10,700 --> 01:08:14,700
You speak of solaronite , but just what is it ?

684
01:08:15,600 --> 01:08:21,600
Take a can of your gasoline . Say this can of gasoline is the sun .

685
01:08:22,800 --> 01:08:28,665
Now you spread a thin a line of it to a ball , representing the Earth .

686
01:08:29,800 --> 01:08:34,800
Now , the gasoline represents the sunlight , the sun particles .

687
01:08:34,900 --> 01:08:39,830
Here we saturate the ball with the gasoline , the sunlight .

688
01:08:40,200 --> 01:08:45,000
Then we put a flame to the ball . The flame will speedily travel around the Earth ,

689
01:08:45,100 --> 01:08:47,700
back along the line of gasoline to can ,

690
01:08:47,800 --> 01:08:52,842
or the sun itself . It will explode this source , and spread

691
01:08:52,942 --> 01:08:57,532
to every place that gasoline , or sunlight , touches .

692
01:08:58,800 --> 01:09:04,495
Explode the sunlight here , Gentlemen , and you explode the universe .

693
01:09:04,500 --> 01:09:10,700
Explode the sunlight here , and a chain reaction will occur , direct to the sun itself .

694
01:09:10,800 --> 01:09:14,800
And to all the planets that sunlight touches .

695
01:09:14,800 --> 01:09:20,070
To every planet in the universe . This why you must be stopped .

696
01:09:21,200 --> 01:09:25,200
This is why any means must be used to stop you .

697
01:09:25,500 --> 01:09:30,500
In a friendly manner , or as it seems , you want it .

698
01:09:31,600 --> 01:09:32,600
He 's mad .

699
01:09:32,700 --> 01:09:37,300
Mad ? Is it mad that you destroy other people to save yourselves ?

700
01:09:37,400 --> 01:09:38,900
You have done this .

701
01:09:39,000 --> 01:09:42,900
Is it mad that one country must destroy another to save themselves ?

702
01:09:43,000 --> 01:09:47,200
You have also done this . How then is it mad that one planet

703
01:09:47,300 --> 01:09:52,248
must destroy another that threatens the very existence -

704
01:09:52,348 --> 01:09:53,600
That 's enough .

705
01:09:53,700 --> 01:09:57,900
In my land , women are for advancing the race , not for fighting

706
01:09:58,000 --> 01:10:03,000
man 's battles . Life is not so expansive on my planet .

707
01:10:03,300 --> 01:10:10,610
We don 't cling to it like you do . Our entire aim is for the development of our planet .

708
01:10:27,300 --> 01:10:29,400
What happened to you ? - How come you 're all alone ?

709
01:10:29,500 --> 01:10:30,863
I asked for lots of help .

710
01:10:30,963 --> 01:10:33,400
You sounded drunk or something on the radio .

711
01:10:33,500 --> 01:10:36,400
If I didn 't see it with my own eyes I would never have believed it .

712
01:10:36,500 --> 01:10:37,500
Believed what ?

713
01:10:37,600 --> 01:10:39,900
It was horrible . And he almost broke my shoulder .

714
01:10:40,000 --> 01:10:42,824
Look , what are you trying to say ? If you don 't make sense

715
01:10:42,924 --> 01:10:45,700
we 'll never get to the bottom of this . Now who slugged you ?

716
01:10:45,800 --> 01:10:47,400
Inspector Clay .

717
01:10:47,500 --> 01:10:48,500
What ?

718
01:10:48,600 --> 01:10:52,700
It was Clay all right , only not like we remembered him .

719
01:10:52,800 --> 01:10:55,500
Well his grave was busted into , wasn 't it ?

720
01:10:55,600 --> 01:10:57,700
Next you 'll tell me you saw skeletons .

721
01:10:57,800 --> 01:11:01,900
We did , earlier . - Now I know you 're off your rocker .

722
01:11:02,000 --> 01:11:05,200
All of us saw , the Lieutenant , the Colonel , everybody .

723
01:11:05,300 --> 01:11:08,000
Where 's the Lieutenant now ? - We 've gotta find them .

724
01:11:08,100 --> 01:11:10,822
Mrs. Trent is gone . I was left here to guard her .

725
01:11:10,922 --> 01:11:13,700
Then Clay showed up and put me out of the running .

726
01:11:13,800 --> 01:11:16,600
And the second time tonight and I 'm getting darned tired of it .

727
01:11:16,700 --> 01:11:19,000
Which way were they going ? - Oh , that way .

728
01:11:19,100 --> 01:11:21,100
Come on .

729
01:11:27,400 --> 01:11:32,300
Then one day it could all be gone , in one big puff of smoke

730
01:11:32,400 --> 01:11:36,400
and ball of fire . All that out there ,

731
01:11:37,200 --> 01:11:40,700
the stars , the planets ,

732
01:11:40,700 --> 01:11:43,800
all just an empty void .

733
01:11:43,800 --> 01:11:46,400
You two had better come along with us .

734
01:11:46,500 --> 01:11:50,500
Come with you ? Where ? - The police station .

735
01:11:53,000 --> 01:11:57,000
So it seems you think you have the upper hand .

736
01:11:57,300 --> 01:11:59,300
Look out there .

737
01:12:04,400 --> 01:12:06,400
Jeff .

738
01:12:16,100 --> 01:12:21,285
She is unharmed , but he would kill in seconds if I so choose .

739
01:12:30,100 --> 01:12:32,100
Holy cow .

740
01:12:39,200 --> 01:12:41,200
Look there .

741
01:12:44,600 --> 01:12:49,200
It 's Clay all right , there 's no mistaking that . - And he 's got Mrs. Trent .

742
01:12:49,300 --> 01:12:50,351
Get your gun ready .

743
01:12:50,451 --> 01:12:53,300
From all I 've seen tonight guns won 't do any good .

744
01:12:53,400 --> 01:12:55,883
Clay is dead , and we buried him . How are we

745
01:12:55,983 --> 01:12:58,300
going to kill somebody that 's already dead ?

746
01:12:58,400 --> 01:13:03,400
Dead . And yet there he stands . That other one earlier I emptied a full clip into him .

747
01:13:03,500 --> 01:13:08,515
I 'm seeing it , that 's the only reason I 'm listening to you .

748
01:13:10,800 --> 01:13:14,800
Look , I 've got an idea . Hurt him or not , we 've got to try something .

749
01:13:14,900 --> 01:13:17,075
I 'm going to sneak up behind him and whop

750
01:13:17,175 --> 01:13:19,400
him over the head . That oughta make him move .

751
01:13:19,500 --> 01:13:23,700
Follow me . Even when Clay was alive he couldn 't run fast enough to catch me ,

752
01:13:23,800 --> 01:13:26,153
so when he does , you grab Mrs. Trent and run

753
01:13:26,253 --> 01:13:28,300
like lightning in the opposite direction .

754
01:13:28,400 --> 01:13:32,990
Oh , you think it will work ? - Know anything else to try ?

755
01:13:48,500 --> 01:13:53,500
Oh , I 'll be all right . Take care of the others .

756
01:13:54,400 --> 01:13:58,100
Your men have felled the big one .

757
01:13:58,100 --> 01:14:01,700
This could only happen because the electrode ray is off .

758
01:14:01,800 --> 01:14:03,700
He 'll walk again when I turn it on .

759
01:14:03,800 --> 01:14:05,400
Hold it , right there .

760
01:14:05,500 --> 01:14:10,253
Suppose the Lieutenant and the others are in that thing .

761
01:14:10,353 --> 01:14:14,943
Well suppose there are martians or something in there .

762
01:14:19,900 --> 01:14:21,900
Come on , let 's go .

763
01:14:23,900 --> 01:14:26,110
Open up in there , open up .

764
01:14:30,500 --> 01:14:32,089
Get that door open .

765
01:14:32,189 --> 01:14:36,280
Colonel I wouldn 't know one switch from another .

766
01:14:49,600 --> 01:14:54,360
Hold on Eros , I 'll have the ship in the air in a minute .

767
01:15:14,000 --> 01:15:17,570
Get out of here , Jeff . The ship 's on fire .

768
01:15:36,700 --> 01:15:38,800
Eros .

769
01:15:38,800 --> 01:15:45,345
Eros everything 's on fire . Hurry , wake up Eros . Eros , Eros , wake up , wake up .

770
01:15:49,900 --> 01:15:53,900
Eros . Eros wake up , Eros . God wake up .

771
01:16:12,200 --> 01:16:15,200
Oh , I wonder if that 's the last we 'll see of them ?

772
01:16:15,300 --> 01:16:18,100
Perhaps , but sooner or later there 'll be other .

773
01:16:18,200 --> 01:16:22,200
Look .

774
01:16:24,300 --> 01:16:27,900
Have they caught that woman , that thing yet ?

775
01:16:28,000 --> 01:16:30,400
Hey that 's right , there 's another ghoul running loose .

776
01:16:30,500 --> 01:16:32,800
And it 's my guess that she 'll look like him .

777
01:16:32,900 --> 01:16:37,745
With the ship and the ray gun gone , they have no control .

778
01:16:37,800 --> 01:16:42,900
We got to hand it to them though , they 're far ahead from us .

779
01:16:46,400 --> 01:16:50,400
Fire . Eros . Aaaaaaaaah .

780
01:16:56,600 --> 01:17:01,600
My friend , you have seen this incident based on sworn testimony .

781
01:17:01,700 --> 01:17:04,600
Can you prove that it didn 't happen ?

782
01:17:04,700 --> 01:17:08,800
Perhaps on your way home , you will pass someone in the dark ,

783
01:17:08,900 --> 01:17:14,170
and you will never know it , for they will be from outer space .

784
01:17:14,600 --> 01:17:19,200
Many scientists believe that another world is watching us this moment .

785
01:17:19,300 --> 01:17:22,100
We once laughed at the horseless carriage ,

786
01:17:22,200 --> 01:17:27,100
the aeroplane , the telephone , the electric light , vitamins ,

787
01:17:27,200 --> 01:17:29,900
radio , and even television .

788
01:17:29,900 --> 01:17:33,900
And now some of us laugh at outer space .

789
01:17:37,800 --> 01:17:41,800
God help us ... in the future .

790
01:18:10,800 --> 01:18:15,800
Base Subtitles by FredFal

